Sequences for the differential test: the same file runs against ween32
(tests/replay_test) and against riched20 on the guest, and the two dumps are
diffed.

The language is tools/vm/replay.h's -- comma-separated `op:a:b`, one line --
which is tests/monkey_test.c's own format. That matters: the monkey's
shrinker already emits it, so a shrunk differential failure is expressible
here without translation, and a shrunk failure is the best report this
project can make.

These seven are alice's weighted shapes and none is arbitrary. Every bug jd
has reported lived in an *interaction* between features rather than in one of
them: a marker clamp that only failed when another marker had moved first, a
toggle that only failed on the first of a run, a word latch set by one of
five gestures and read by all, an armed format that failed to close a typed
run. A sequence that only types cannot find any of them.

Three of them wrap on purpose. Dan's swapped ruler markers and my own first
two bullet captures were each invisible until a second line existed -- a
sample that does not wrap looks exactly like one that does and says nothing.

`type` carries a character code, so a word is one op per letter. That is
verbose to read and is the format the generator emits; the comment at the top
of each file says what the sequence is for, since the ops do not.
